        text: "For most of its industrial history, Gujarat's reputation was built on chemicals, textiles, and petrochemicals, the unglamorous, high-volume manufacturing that rarely gets magazine covers but quietly generates an enormous share of India's industrial output. The Gujarat Industrial Development Corporation, GIDC, built its estates in Vapi, Ankleshwar, and dozens of other towns around exactly that kind of manufacturing, and for decades, that was Gujarat's industrial identity: reliable, high-volume, not especially glamorous.",
