        text: "The strategic lesson here, for enterprise leaders evaluating where to locate manufacturing investment, is that sector diversity within a single industrial corridor is not a dilution of focus; done well, it is a hedge against the single-sector risk that corridors like Pune's auto-heavy belt inevitably carry. When global automotive demand softens, a corridor built entirely around automotive manufacturing feels that softness across its entire local economy, its component suppliers, its logistics providers, its labor market. A corridor with genuine depth in two distinct sectors absorbs that kind of downturn differently, because the electronics side of the local economy isn't necessarily moving in the same cycle as the automotive side. Tamil Nadu didn't plan this diversification as a risk-management strategy from the outset, but it has become one of the corridor's quiet structural advantages as global manufacturing demand has grown less predictable in recent years.",
