      "What the Sriperumbudur-Oragadam story ultimately offers the rest of India's industrial map is a working example of diversification done at the corridor level rather than the company level. Most manufacturing strategy conversations about diversification happen inside a single company, across its own product lines or its own supplier base. Tamil Nadu's corridor shows what it looks like when an entire industrial geography diversifies instead, two sectors, one shared infrastructure base, and a resilience that neither sector could have built entirely on its own.",
